    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T22:30:46Z",
    "body": "Judgement calls for the maintainer (also in docs/decisions/255-structural-ui-tests.md):\n1. **The snapshot lane runs in debug, filtered by `snapshot`.** Debug because the goldens were always made from debug runs. The filter keeps the two ignored playback benches (`play_bench_tests.rs`) out of it; they were not in the release tier before either.\n2. **No loose \"renders non-blank\" pixel test.** The issue's optional step 3 is skipped, because any pixel test brings platform noise back into the PR lane.\n3. **The painted strips are checked by their painted text, not AccessKit.** The ribbon, browser rows and dock tabs have no accessibility nodes, and adding them would be a product change. Say if you'd rather have them as AccessKit nodes in a follow-up.\n4. **One PR changes both tests and process.** AGENTS.md, the PR-reviewer agent and the review-prs skill change here alongside the tests.\n5. **On macOS the lane fails on an unchanged tree** (`_light` 1 px over, `tool_editor` 6 px). Run it at the cut on the OS that made the goldens.",
